**Job Description**
-------------------


**International Sales has an opening for a****Business Development Executive, Specialty** **to be** **based in our** **India office.**



To support the continued business growth of our Specialty Industries in APAC, we seek a highly motivated and driven individual to be part of the New Business Development team. Reporting to Simon Baker\-Chambers Staff VP, Global Sales, EMEA and APAC, this individual will be responsible to grow the Specialty Industries book including Chemical, Renewables and Forest Products business.



In this position, the individual will be expected to solicit new business both directly with prospective clients, as well as in collaboration with key broker partners.



**Key Responsibilities:**


* Achieve new business objectives as established by the Regional Sales Manager;
* Develop strategy and complete call plans / reports to ensure that all prospects’ information and documentation are updated in SRS (Strategic Relationship System);
* Build and maintain excellent relationships with prospective clients and brokers to successfully create continuous new business opportunities;
* Manage new business opportunities by continuously developing prospects;
* Maintain an active involvement in the local insurance and brokerage community by participating in meetings, conferences and industry\-related functions;
* Maintain a thorough understanding of competitors’ products, services, current pricing strategy and practices.



**Qualifications**  





* A Bachelor’s degree in any discipline;
* At least 10 years’ working experience in risk management, loss prevention engineering, claims or underwriting;
* Experience in the broader insurance industry is desired but not essential;
* Knowledge of sales processes (prospecting, nurturing, follow\-up, follow\-through, negotiating, closing) and proven sales experience is a plus;
* Ability to develop strong relationships with clients;
* Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English
* Excellent interpersonal skills, including facilitating and presentation;
* Excellent planning, organizational and time management skills;
* Technology and social media savvy, including proficiency in Microsoft office software

**Responsibilities**
* According to the company\& business development plan, please independently complete the maintenance of the EMU video system assigned by the competent Railway Bureau to ensure the normal operation of the system;
* Identify hardware faults and carry out on\-site maintenance;
* Sign the after\-sales service report.
* Collect equipment fault information;
* Feedback the fault information of the equipment to the engineering department, which will send it to the quality department, R \& D department and other relevant departments to provide accurate reference for the company's product performance improvement.
* Properly handle the relationship with Party A and maintain the good image of the company;
* Provide on\-site training for customers and complete all specified tasks.
* With the improvement of your technical ability, you will gradually become a technical support engineer or senior technical support engineer.


**Requirement**
* Master the basic theoretical knowledge of computer network
* Understand the basic knowledge of electronic circuits
* Familiar with news and knowledge of multimedia audio\-visual industry
* More than three years of after\-sales service or related work experience, able to independently complete equipment installation, debugging, hardware product fault identification and on\-site maintenance.
* Good English listening, speaking, reading and writing skills;
* Familiar with basic computer operation, able to use AutoCAD, Visio and other drawing software.;
* Good at language expression and communication with customers.


